I can't answer this from the excerpts. The part of section 43 that sets the processor-to-controller notification deadline isn't included.

The Data Protection Act excerpt from the breach provisions (Law/act-part-04b-obligations-and-breach.md) starts at line 143, in the middle of section 43. It covers only:
- the content of the notice to the data subject (lines 143-153);
- the exemption where safeguards such as encryption are in place (line 155);
- phased provision of information (line 157);
- the controller's duty to record the facts, effects and remedial action (lines 159-165).

None of these lines say how soon a processor must notify the controller. The regulations excerpt (Law/general-regs-part-06-breach-notification.md:33-57) deals with what a controller's notification to the Data Commissioner must contain. It gives no hour limit for a processor either.

To find the figure, you would need the earlier lines of section 43 in act-part-04b-obligations-and-breach.md, which I wasn't shown.
